{"step_index":80,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T18:32:05Z","thinking":"**Planning graph counterexample search**\n\nConsidering testing the conjecture `radius + 1 <= roman_domination_number` by generating various graph types. This includes connected graphs of small sizes (2-8 vertices), trees (up to 15 vertices), random graphs, and diameter-critical graphs. The strategy involves writing a Python script to compute the Roman domination number and radius for each graph type and checking for counterexamples. The script will be executed using a command execution tool.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/.venv/bin/python -c '\nimport networkx as nx\nfrom itertools import product\n\ndef roman_dom(G):\n    # compute roman domination number\n    nodes = list(G.nodes())\n    n = len(nodes)\n    best = 2 * n\n    for f in product([0, 1, 2], repeat=n):\n        # check if roman dominating\n        valid = True\n        for i, u in enumerate(nodes):\n            if f[i] == 0:\n                # must have neighbor with 2\n                has_two = any(f[nodes.index(v)] == 2 for v in G.neighbors(u))\n                if not has_two:\n                    valid = False\n                    break\n        if valid:\n            cost = sum(f)\n            if cost < best:\n                best = cost\n    return best\n\nbad = []\nfor n in range(2, 7):\n    for G in nx.graph_atlas_g():\n        if len(G) == n and nx.is_connected(G):\n            rad = nx.radius(G)\n            rd = roman_dom(G)\n            if rad + 1 > rd:\n                bad.append((n, rad, rd, list(G.edges())))\n                print(f\"COUNTEREXAMPLE: n={n}, rad={rad}, rd={rd}, edges={list(G.edges())}\")\n\nprint(f\"Total counterexamples up to n=6: {len(bad)}\")\n'","Cwd":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9","WaitMsBeforeAsync":10000,"toolAction":"Searching for counterexamples up to n=6","toolSummary":"Search atlas for counterexamples"}}]}
