{"step_index":82,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T18:32:09Z","thinking":"**Exploring larger graph structures**\n\nConsidering scaling up the graph size for testing, specifically exploring trees with up to twenty nodes. Need to understand the definition of 'roman_domination_number' in a known library. The definition seems to be in a file named `reference/GraphInvariantsComputable.lean`. The file's contents include a definition related to a \"IsRomanDominatingFunction\".\n\n\n**Analyzing graph radius definition**\n\nThe code defines `romanDominationNumber` using a function `romanWeight` on a Roman dominating function. The definition of radius relies on `ballWithin`, which recursively computes the set of vertices reachable within a given distance.  `eccentricity` calculates the shortest distance from a vertex to all other vertices.\n\n`radius` computes the minimum eccentricity across all vertices in the graph, representing the smallest value $k$ such that every vertex in the graph is within distance $k$ of some vertex.  The `HasRadius` property indicates if the graph has a defined radius.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/.venv/bin/python -c '\nimport networkx as nx\nimport scipy\n\ndef roman_dom_lp(G):\n    # MIP using scipy.optimize.milp\n    import numpy as np\n    from scipy.optimize import milp, LinearConstraint\n    nodes = list(G.nodes())\n    n = len(nodes)\n    node_to_i = {u: i for i, u in enumerate(nodes)}\n    # variables: x_u in {0,1}, y_u in {0,1}, f(u) = x_u + 2*y_u\n    # x_u + y_u <= 1\n    # x_u + y_u + sum_{v in N(u)} y_v >= 1\n    # objective: min sum (x_u + 2*y_u)\n    # variables: 2*n vars, [x_0, ..., x_{n-1}, y_0, ..., y_{n-1}]\n    c = np.array([1.0]*n + [2.0]*n)\n    \n    # constraint 1: x_u + y_u <= 1 -> (n constraints)\n    A1 = np.zeros((n, 2*n))\n    for i in range(n):\n        A1[i, i] = 1.0\n        A1[i, n + i] = 1.0\n    lc1 = LinearConstraint(A1, -np.inf, np.ones(n))\n    \n    # constraint 2: x_u + y_u + sum_{v in N(u)} y_v >= 1\n    A2 = np.zeros((n, 2*n))\n    for i, u in enumerate(nodes):\n        A2[i, i] = 1.0\n        A2[i, n + i] = 1.0\n        for v in G.neighbors(u):\n            A2[i, n + node_to_i[v]] = 1.0\n    lc2 = LinearConstraint(A2, np.ones(n), np.inf*np.ones(n))\n    \n    integrality = np.ones(2*n)\n    bounds = scipy.optimize.Bounds(0, 1)\n    res = milp(c, integrality=integrality, constraints=[lc1, lc2], bounds=bounds)\n    return int(round(res.fun))\n\n# test on random trees and graphs\nimport random\nrandom.seed(42)\nfor trial in range(100):\n    n = random.randint(5, 30)\n    G = nx.random_labeled_tree(n)\n    rad = nx.radius(G)\n    rd = roman_dom_lp(G)\n    if rad + 1 > rd:\n        print(f\"TREE COUNTEREXAMPLE! n={n}, rad={rad}, rd={rd}\")\n        break\n\nfor trial in range(100):\n    n = random.randint(5, 20)\n    p = random.uniform(0.1, 0.5)\n    G = nx.erdos_renyi_graph(n, p)\n    if nx.is_connected(G):\n        rad = nx.radius(G)\n        rd = roman_dom_lp(G)\n        if rad + 1 > rd:\n            print(f\"RANDOM GRAPH COUNTEREXAMPLE! n={n}, rad={rad}, rd={rd}\")\n            break\n\nprint(\"All tests passed, 0 counterexamples.\")\n'","Cwd":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9","WaitMsBeforeAsync":10000,"toolAction":"Testing random trees and graphs with MIP","toolSummary":"Run MIP tests for counterexamples"}}]}
