{"step_index":95,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T18:32:38Z","thinking":"**Assessing goal and approach**\n\nThe goal is to show the radius plus one is less than or equal to the Roman domination number of the graph. The strategy suggests using `le_romanDominationNumber G (GraphCalc.radius G + 1)`. This means proving for all functions from vertices to Fin 3, the graph is Roman dominating.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/.venv/bin/python -c '\nimport networkx as nx\nfrom itertools import product\n\ndef test_graphs():\n    for n in range(2, 7):\n        for G in nx.graph_atlas_g():\n            if len(G) == n and nx.is_connected(G):\n                nodes = list(G.nodes())\n                # test all minimal Roman dominating functions\n                for f in product([0, 1, 2], repeat=n):\n                    # check valid\n                    valid = True\n                    for i, u in enumerate(nodes):\n                        if f[i] == 0:\n                            if not any(f[nodes.index(v)] == 2 for v in G.neighbors(u)):\n                                valid = False\n                                break\n                    if not valid:\n                        continue\n                    wt = sum(f)\n                    # check if there is some vertex with ecc + 1 <= wt\n                    eccs = [nx.eccentricity(G, v) for v in nodes]\n                    if not any(e + 1 <= wt for e in eccs):\n                        print(f\"FAILED: n={n}, wt={wt}, eccs={eccs}, edges={list(G.edges())}, f={f}\")\n                        return False\n    print(\"ALL GRAPHS UP TO N=6 HAVE A VERTEX WITH ecc(v) + 1 <= weight(f)!\")\n    return True\n\ntest_graphs()\n'","Cwd":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9","WaitMsBeforeAsync":10000,"toolAction":"Checking existence of vertex with ecc + 1 <= weight","toolSummary":"Check vertex ecc bound in python"}}]}
