{"step_index":114,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T18:37:09Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-11T20:37:09+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-11T20:37:09+02:00\n\nThe command exited with code 0.\nOutput:\n1: /-\r\n2: Copyright (c) 2022 Kyle Miller. All rights reserved.\r\n3: Released under Apache 2.0 license as described in the file LICENSE.\r\n4: Authors: Kyle Miller, Vincent Beffara, Rida Hamadani, Nelson Spence\r\n5: -/\r\n6: module\r\n7: \r\n8: public import Mathlib.Combinatorics.SimpleGraph.Connectivity.Connected\r\n9: public import Mathlib.Data.ENat.Lattice\r\n10: \r\n11: /-!\r\n12: # Graph metric\r\n13: \r\n14: This module defines the `SimpleGraph.edist` function, which takes pairs of vertices to the length of\r\n15: the shortest walk between them, or `⊤` if they are disconnected. It also defines `SimpleGraph.dist`\r\n16: which is the `ℕ`-valued version of `SimpleGraph.edist`, and `SimpleGraph.ball` which is the open\r\n17: ball in the graph extended metric.\r\n18: \r\n19: ## Main definitions\r\n20: \r\n21: - `SimpleGraph.edist` is the graph extended metric.\r\n22: - `SimpleGraph.dist` is the graph metric.\r\n23: - `SimpleGraph.ball` is the open ball of a given radius around a vertex.\r\n24: \r\n25: ## TODO\r\n26: \r\n27: - Provide an additional computable version of `SimpleGraph.dist`\r\n28:   for when `G` is connected.\r\n29: \r\n30: - When directed graphs exist, a directed notion of distance,\r\n31:   likely `ENat`-valued.\r\n32: \r\n33: ## Tags\r\n34: \r\n35: graph metric, distance, ball\r\n36: \r\n37: -/\r\n38: \r\n39: @[expose] public section\r\n40: \r\n41: assert_not_exists Field\r\n42: \r\n43: namespace SimpleGraph\r\n44: \r\n45: variable {V : Type*} (G : SimpleGraph V)\r\n46: \r\n47: /-! ## Metric -/\r\n48: \r\n49: section edist\r\n50: \r\n51: /--\r\n52: The extended distance between two vertices is the length of the shortest walk between them.\r\n53: It is `⊤` if no such walk exists.\r\n54: -/\r\n55: noncomputable def edist (u v : V) : ℕ∞ :=\r\n56:   ⨅ w : G.Walk u v, w.length\r\n57: \r\n58: variable {G} {u v w : V}\r\n59: \r\n60: theorem edist_eq_sInf : G.edist u v = sInf (Set.range fun w : G.Walk u v ↦ (w.length : ℕ∞)) := rfl\r\n61: \r\n62: protected theorem Reachable.exists_walk_length_eq_edist (hr : G.Reachable u v) :\r\n63:     ∃ p : G.Walk u v, p.length = G.edist u v :=\r\n64:   csInf_mem <| Set.range_nonempty_iff_nonempty.mpr hr\r\n65: \r\n66: protected theorem Connected.exists_walk_length_eq_edist (hconn : G.Connected) (u v : V) :\r\n67:     ∃ p : G.Walk u v, p.length = G.edist u v :=\r\n68:   (hconn u v).exists_walk_length_eq_edist\r\n69: \r\n70: theorem edist_le (p : G.Walk u v) :\r\n71:     G.edist u v ≤ p.length :=\r\n72:   sInf_le ⟨p, rfl⟩\r\n73: protected alias Walk.edist_le := edist_le\r\n74: \r\n75: @[simp]\r\n76: theorem edist_eq_zero_iff : G.edist u v = 0 ↔ u = v := by\r\n77:   simp [edist]\r\n78: \r\n79: @[simp]\r\n80: theorem edist_self : edist G v v = 0 :=\r\n81:   edist_eq_zero_iff.mpr rfl\r\n82: \r\n83: theorem edist_pos_of_ne (hne : u ≠ v) :\r\n84:     0 < G.edist u v :=\r\n85:   pos_iff_ne_zero.mpr <| edist_eq_zero_iff.ne.mpr hne\r\n86: \r\n87: lemma edist_eq_top_of_not_reachable (h : ¬G.Reachable u v) :\r\n88:     G.edist u v = ⊤ := by\r\n89:   simp [edist, not_reachable_iff_isEmpty_walk.mp h]\r\n90: \r\n91: theorem reachable_of_edist_ne_top (h : G.edist u v ≠ ⊤) :\r\n92:     G.Reachable u v :=\r\n93:   not_not.mp <| edist_eq_top_of_not_reachable.mt h\r\n94: \r\n95: lemma exists_walk_of_edist_ne_top (h : G.edist u v ≠ ⊤) :\r\n96:     ∃ p : G.Walk u v, p.length = G.edist u v :=\r\n97:   (reachable_of_edist_ne_top h).exists_walk_length_eq_edist\r\n98: \r\n99: protected theorem edist_triangle : G.edist u w ≤ G.edist u v + G.edist v w := by\r\n100:   cases eq_or_ne (G.edist u v) ⊤ with\r\n\n"}
