{"step_index":116,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T18:37:11Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-11T20:37:11+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-11T20:37:11+02:00\n\nThe command exited with code 0.\nOutput:\n1: /-\r\n2: Copyright (c) 2024 Rida Hamadani. All rights reserved.\r\n3: Released under Apache 2.0 license as described in the file LICENSE.\r\n4: Authors: Rida Hamadani\r\n5: -/\r\n6: module\r\n7: \r\n8: public import Mathlib.Combinatorics.SimpleGraph.Metric\r\n9: \r\n10: /-!\r\n11: # Diameter of a simple graph\r\n12: \r\n13: This module defines the eccentricity of vertices, the diameter, and the radius of a simple graph.\r\n14: \r\n15: ## Main definitions\r\n16: \r\n17: - `SimpleGraph.eccent`: the eccentricity of a vertex in a simple graph, which is the maximum\r\n18:   distances between it and the other vertices.\r\n19: \r\n20: - `SimpleGraph.ediam`: the graph extended diameter, which is the maximum eccentricity.\r\n21:   It is `ℕ∞`-valued.\r\n22: \r\n23: - `SimpleGraph.diam`: the graph diameter, an `ℕ`-valued version of `SimpleGraph.ediam`.\r\n24: \r\n25: - `SimpleGraph.radius`: the graph radius, which is the minimum eccentricity. It is `ℕ∞`-valued.\r\n26: \r\n27: - `SimpleGraph.center`: the set of vertices with eccentricity equal to the graph's radius.\r\n28: \r\n29: -/\r\n30: \r\n31: @[expose] public section\r\n32: \r\n33: assert_not_exists Field\r\n34: \r\n35: namespace SimpleGraph\r\n36: variable {α : Type*} {G G' : SimpleGraph α}\r\n37: \r\n38: section eccent\r\n39: \r\n40: /-- The eccentricity of a vertex is the greatest distance between it and any other vertex. -/\r\n41: noncomputable def eccent (G : SimpleGraph α) (u : α) : ℕ∞ :=\r\n42:   ⨆ v, G.edist u v\r\n43: \r\n44: lemma eccent_def : G.eccent = fun u ↦ ⨆ v, G.edist u v := rfl\r\n45: \r\n46: lemma edist_le_eccent {u v : α} : G.edist u v ≤ G.eccent u :=\r\n47:   le_iSup (G.edist u) v\r\n48: \r\n49: lemma exists_edist_eq_eccent_of_finite [Finite α] (u : α) :\r\n50:     ∃ v, G.edist u v = G.eccent u :=\r\n51:   have : Nonempty α := Nonempty.intro u\r\n52:   exists_eq_ciSup_of_finite\r\n53: \r\n54: lemma eccent_eq_top_of_not_connected (h : ¬ G.Connected) (u : α) :\r\n55:     G.eccent u = ⊤ := by\r\n56:   rw [connected_iff_exists_forall_reachable] at h\r\n57:   push Not at h\r\n58:   obtain ⟨v, h⟩ := h u\r\n59:   rw [eq_top_iff, ← edist_eq_top_of_not_reachable h]\r\n60:   exact le_iSup (G.edist u) v\r\n61: \r\n62: lemma eccent_eq_zero_of_subsingleton [Subsingleton α] (u : α) : G.eccent u = 0 := by\r\n63:   simpa [eccent, edist_eq_zero_iff] using subsingleton_iff.mp ‹_› u\r\n64: \r\n65: lemma eccent_ne_zero [Nontrivial α] (u : α) : G.eccent u ≠ 0 := by\r\n66:   obtain ⟨v, huv⟩ := exists_ne ‹_›\r\n67:   contrapose huv\r\n68:   simp only [eccent, ENat.iSup_eq_zero, edist_eq_zero_iff] at huv\r\n69:   exact (huv v).symm\r\n70: \r\n71: lemma eccent_eq_zero_iff (u : α) : G.eccent u = 0 ↔ Subsingleton α := by\r\n72:   refine ⟨fun h ↦ ?_, fun _ ↦ eccent_eq_zero_of_subsingleton u⟩\r\n73:   contrapose! h\r\n74:   exact eccent_ne_zero u\r\n75: \r\n76: lemma eccent_pos_iff (u : α) : 0 < G.eccent u ↔ Nontrivial α := by\r\n77:   rw [pos_iff_ne_zero, ← not_subsingleton_iff_nontrivial, ← eccent_eq_zero_iff]\r\n78: \r\n79: @[simp]\r\n80: lemma eccent_bot [Nontrivial α] (u : α) : (⊥ : SimpleGraph α).eccent u = ⊤ :=\r\n81:   eccent_eq_top_of_not_connected not_connected_bot u\r\n82: \r\n83: @[simp]\r\n84: lemma eccent_top [Nontrivial α] (u : α) : (⊤ : SimpleGraph α).eccent u = 1 := by\r\n85:   apply le_antisymm ?_ <| Order.one_le_iff_pos.mpr <| pos_iff_ne_zero.mpr <| eccent_ne_zero u\r\n86:   rw [eccent, iSup_le_iff]\r\n87:   intro v\r\n88:   cases eq_or_ne u v <;> simp_all [edist_top_of_ne]\r\n89: \r\n90: lemma eq_top_iff_forall_eccent_eq_one [Nontrivial α] :\r\n91:     G = ⊤ ↔ ∀ u, G.eccent u = 1 := by\r\n92:   refine ⟨fun h ↦ h ▸ eccent_top, fun h ↦ ?_⟩\r\n93:   ext u v\r\n94:   refine ⟨Adj.ne, fun huv ↦ ?_⟩\r\n95:   rw [← edist_eq_one_iff_adj]\r\n96:   apply le_antisymm ((h u).symm ▸ edist_le_eccent)\r\n97:   rw [Order.one_le_iff_pos, pos_iff_ne_zero, edist_eq_zero_iff.ne]\r\n98:   exact huv.ne\r\n99: \r\n100: lemma eccent_le_iff (u : α) (k : ℕ∞) : G.eccent u ≤ k ↔ ∀ v, G.edist u v ≤ k :=\r\n\n"}
{"step_index":117,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T18:37:11Z","thinking":"**Differentiating Graph Radius Definitions**\n\nAttempting to resolve a potential naming conflict; `GraphCalc.radius` isn't `SimpleGraph.radius`. Examining the definition of `GraphCalc.radius` within the relevant file shows it is defined using a `ballWithin` function and utilizes the graph's adjacency relation. This helps clarify the intended meaning and context.\n\n\n**Formulating proof strategy**\n\nConsidering how to prove the `Candidate` property, focusing on relating the graph radius and roman domination number. The core idea involves showing `GraphCalc.radius G + 1 ≤ GraphCalc.romanWeight f` for a Roman dominating function. This requires leveraging available lemmas and definitions to establish the inequality.\n\n\n**Establishing a lower bound**\n\nTrying to prove `GraphCalc.radius G ≤ GraphCalc.romanWeight f - 1`. Need to first understand `romanWeight f`. Can it be 0 or 1 for a nontrivial graph? No, since it's a Roman dominating function, weight 0 or 1 leads to contradictions. Therefore, the weight must be at least 2.\n\nConsidering a Lean lemma: proving `2 ≤ GraphCalc.romanWeight f`. If the sum is less than 2, then it's either 0 or 1, and no vertex can be 2. If no vertex is 2, then no vertex can be 0 (due to domination). That leads to the contradiction that every vertex must be at least 1, implying the sum is at least the graph's cardinality (which is at least 2). This contradiction confirms the lower bound.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"grep -rn \"ballWithin\" /mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/lean_project","Cwd":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Searching for ballWithin in lean_project","toolSummary":"Grep ballWithin"}}]}
